21. Database Requirements

The system should use a proper relational database.

Important entities may include:

- admins
- students
- teachers
- classes
- student_fees
- teacher_salaries
- attendance
- user_accounts
- student_accounts
- teacher_accounts
- payment_records

Use proper relationships and foreign keys where supported.

Do not store everything in one database table.

---

22. Financial Logic

The system must clearly separate:

Income

Student fee payments.

Expenses

Teacher salary payments.

Net Income

Net Income = Total Fee Income - Total Teacher Salary

All calculations must be generated automatically from database records.

Do not manually hard-code financial totals.

---

23. Data Integrity

The system must ensure:

- Unique Student IDs
- Unique Teacher IDs
- No duplicate attendance for the same student/date unless explicitly allowed
- No accidental duplicate monthly fee records
- No invalid negative payment amounts
- No invalid salary amounts
- Proper class assignment
- Proper account-to-student/teacher relationship

Use database validation and server-side validation.

